airplay: drop transport commands from the speaker's event channel

A HomePod's touch surface sends play, pause, next and previous over
the AirPlay event channel as sendMediaRemoteCommand, and owntone
applied them to its player. With a pipe as the source that is
destructive: pause closes and reopens the pipe, the process writing
it (librespot) gets EPIPE and exits, and play then restarts the item
at position 0. Next and previous mean nothing inside a pipe.

Drop them, at INFO, and leave it to the client driving this server to
decide what the speaker's controls should do.

--- a/src/outputs/airplay_events.c
+++ b/src/outputs/airplay_events.c
@@ -333,6 +333,17 @@
 {
   struct player_status status;
 
+  // The player's source is a pipe fed by another process. Pausing closes and
+  // reopens the pipe, which the writer sees as EPIPE and dies of, and playing
+  // again restarts the item from position 0. Next and previous mean nothing
+  // inside a pipe. So the speaker's own transport controls are dropped here,
+  // and the client driving this server decides what they should do.
+  if (event != AIRPLAY_EVENT_UNKNOWN)
+    {
+      DPRINTF(E_INFO, L_AIRPLAY, "Dropping media remote command from speaker (event %d)\n", event);
+      return;
+    }
+
   player_get_status(&status);
 
   switch (event)
